  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvemo Kartli Solid Waste Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The provision of a sovereign loan increase of up to EUR 6 million to finance  the funding gap for the construction of an EU-compliant regional sanitary  landfill in Kvemo Kartli region and the purchase of specialised equipment for  related landfill operations (the &quot;Project&quot;).  The loan was originally signed in 2015 in the amount of EUR 7 million (in two  tranches) to finance the construction of the Kvemo Kartli landfill and  specialised equipment, which continues to be financed by EBRD, and relevant  infrastructure in Marneuli municipality, which will now be financed by the  Government of Georgia.  Based on updated scope, the EBRD financing is provided in two tranches: EUR  4.3 million from the original loan provided in 2015 and EUR 6 million from the  loan increase provided in 2024.  The Project aims to introduce a modern solid waste management system covering  the collection and EU-compliant disposal of municipal solid waste and is  expected to provide major environmental and social benefits for approximately  300,000 people in the Kvemo Kartli region. The Project is part of the National  Waste Management Strategy Action Plan and is a part of a broader programme  aiming to assist the country to meet its obligations under the European Union  Association Agreement, signed between Georgia and the EU in 2014, which  includes obligations to improve solid waste management in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
